Switch: give guest memory back to the heap when the game frees it.

The guest heaps' Release/Decommit never reached the host, so on Switch every guest page ever
touched stayed backed by heap memory: a session through training and a mission reached 3185 of
3189 MB, and leaving to the menu then failed to create a thread (C0000017) and hung on a black
screen. BaseHeap::Release/Decommit now call DeallocFixed, which frees the committed chunks
entirely inside the range (RexGmDecommit, also made to look only at the chunks in the range).
--switch_release_guest_memory=false restores the old behaviour.

